	  descent, dead-node restart, and RCU lifecycle behind mtree_load().

	  Maple node encoding, node layout, protected slot access, tracepoint
	  emission, and lockdep checks remain in C. The exported C entry point
	  remains as an ABI adapter. The C fallback retains the complete load
	  traversal.

	  This is part of the experimental native Rust kernel migration.
	  If unsure, say Y.

config RUST_PERCPU_REFCOUNT
	bool "Rust implementation of percpu_ref() lifecycle"
	depends on RUST
	default y
	help
	  Use Rust for the production lifecycle state machine of percpu_ref().
	  This includes initialization, mode switching, kill confirmation, exit,
	  reinitialization, and resurrection.

	  The per-CPU get/put fast paths remain inline C because they depend on
	  architecture-specific atomic and per-CPU primitives.

	  This is part of the experimental native Rust kernel migration.
	  If unsure, say Y.

